# caddy reverse proxy for gatho ha example
#
# each gatho server instance gets its own caddy in front of it.
# rooms spawn on os-assigned ephemeral ports. clients connect through
# caddy using the port number as a path prefix:
#
#   ws://localhost:{caddy_port}/{room_port}?token=...
#
# caddy extracts the port from the path, strips it, and reverse-proxies
# to the host machine at that port. websocket upgrades are handled automatically.
#
# env vars:
#   CADDY_PORT      — the port caddy listens on
#   UPSTREAM_HOST   — the host to proxy to (host.docker.internal on mac, localhost on linux)

:{$CADDY_PORT}

# path is always /{port} or /{port}/ — we just need to strip the port prefix.
# the room's ws server listens on /* so rewriting to / is always correct.
@room path_regexp room ^/(\d+)
reverse_proxy @room {$UPSTREAM_HOST}:{re.room.1} {
	rewrite /
}
